  "hints": [
    "Neither the matrix nor the vectors can ever be expanded: the dimensions reach a billion. Every operation has to touch only stored non-zero entries.",
    "For M·v, the only matrix entries that matter are those in the columns where v is non-zero; for vᵀ·M, those in the rows where v is non-zero. A single storage layout makes one of these cheap and the other expensive.",
    "Keeping two indexes of the same entries, one grouped by column and one grouped by row, makes both products cheap; the price is that every set has to update both consistently, including removing an entry when its value becomes zero."
  ],
